  "readmeFile": "readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## v6.0.0 Major feature release\n\n### Bird view\n\n- 10, 11 is now supported, interim .net versions dropped and net45 -> net472, netstandard2.0 -> netstandard2.1\n- Decrease memory footprint without speed regression\n- Remove Obsolete API (small things in more customizable parts of Container)\n- Compile-time Dependency Injection (T4-based, AOT-friendly; see `readme.md` in the DryIoc.dll NuGet package)\n- #492 Remove obsolete WithAutoFallbackResolution\n\n### Features\n\n- #695 Improve DryIoc.dll NuGet package CompileTime DI install/update experience\n- #679 Add DryIoc own all-encompassing RegisterAttribute\n- #676 Add the Settings.ThrowOnRegisteringDisposableTransient on the registration level to override the global setting\n- #660 Populate on IRegistrator\n- #638 Add the global test option to run all tests with WithoutUseInterpretation option\n- #636 [question/feature request] keyed services in delegate resolution\n- #632 MS DI AddKeyed... variant registration fails\n- #618 Multiple same service key support mostly for DryIoc.MS.DI though it is already supported in DryIoc.MefAttributedModel\n- #612 For the conditional singleton or the singleton registered with AnyKey - should we create a new singleton per condition or the resolution key?\n- #512 Optimize injection of IResolverContext\n- #504 Probably add the IDictionary<TServiceKey, TService> wrapper\n- #503 [CompTimeDI] Replace partial methods with more flexible interface ICompileTimeContainer\n- #495 [CompTimeDI] Automatically generate Resolution calls for the missing registrations to avoid manual RegisterPlaceholder\n- #485 Add Rules to IResolverContext interface\n- #480 Change Request.Container property to field and change its type from IContainer to Container\n- #223 IAsyncDisposable is not being called after container.Dispose\n- #212 Improve source package with T4 install experience\n\n### Fixes\n\n- #708 Missed parent parameter in IContainer.With overload\n- #694 Singleton service resolved by scoped container, not root container\n- #692 Resolve failed on Android(Avalonia)\n- #690 DryIoc is not working together with Blazor InputFile component\n- #685 Creating scopes via funcs is not thread-safe and fails sporadically with NullRef exception\n- #672 Wrong decorator parameter with custom args\n- #653 KeyValuePair exposes internal DryIoc structures\n- #651 Resolving func-wrapper when having circular-dependency throws RecursiveDependencyDetected\n- #648 [BUG] Resolve<> crashes with the misleading, casting-related Exception when class is also registered using RegisterInitializer\n- #646 Resolve enforces passed arguments to be used (and fails because of it)\n- #643 WithConcreteTypeDynamicRegistrations results in unintended instantiation\n- #642 System.NullReferenceException: Object reference not set to an instance of an object\n- #631 Conditional registrations\n- #625 FactoryType is not forwarded in the RegisterMapping<TService, TRegisteredService> method\n- #624 Consistent behavior of a faulty singleton\n- #623 Scoped service decorator\n- #610 ConstructorWithResolvableArguments conflicts with dynamic registrations\n- #580 Scope is lost in IResolver inside scope because of singleton\n- #535 Property injection is not working correctly when appending a new implementation for multiple registrations of the same interface and injecting an enumerable of the interface.\n- #552 Compatibility with Android/iOS AOT compilation\n- #532 [Xamarin.iOS] DryIocTypeResolver.Resolve (System.Type type) SIGABRT: Operation is not supported on this platform.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": false,
